=== SIGNATURE ===
str_rev(str)

=== COMMENT ===
Reverses a string (character by character), respecting whole multi-character symbols.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(str,
   IF(
      ROWS(str) * COLUMNS(str) = 1,
      LET(one, CONCAT(str), TEXTJOIN("", , MID(one, SEQUENCE(LEN(one), , LEN(one), -1), 1))),
      MAP(
         str,
         LAMBDA(x, LET(one, CONCAT(x), TEXTJOIN("", , MID(one, SEQUENCE(LEN(one), , LEN(one), -1), 1))))
      )
   )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Reverses the characters of a string.

Arguments:
  str - the text to reverse.

A single value that arrives as a 1x1 array (TOCOL(x), {x}, a one-cell FILTER/INDEX result) is collapsed to a scalar first, so it behaves exactly like the plain value.

Returns:
  The string reversed. Works on arrays of strings.

Example:
  str_rev("abc")  ->  "cba"
